<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        A fixture is one light. It tells Lanyard which channels the light uses and what each one does, so the
        desk can show it as a card with brightness and colour controls. Press <strong>Fixtures</strong> on the desk.
    </FluentText>
    <ol>
        <li>Give the fixture a <strong>Name</strong> and its <strong>Start Channel</strong> (the DMX address set on the light).</li>
        <li>Choose the <strong>Fixture type</strong> from one of:
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Saved types</strong>: ones you've used before.</li>
                <li><strong>Open Fixture Library</strong>: search by manufacturer or model, then choose the
                    <strong>Mode</strong> the light is set to.</li>
                <li><strong>Import a file</strong>: a fixture file in the Open Fixture Library JSON format, downloaded
                    from open-fixture-library.org.</li>
                <li><strong>Build your own</strong>: list the light's channels from its manual. It's saved under Saved
                    types for next time.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Press <strong>Add Fixture</strong>. Edit or delete fixtures from the same list.</li>
    </ol>
</HelpTab>
